1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,338
Smart contracts do not fail because their interface looks wrong.

2
00:00:03,288 --> 00:00:07,730
They fail because deployed behavior, permissions, and accounting assumptions break under pressure.

3
00:00:07,730 --> 00:00:14,548
This is BOT Chain Crash Lab: a live, read-only contract investigation workspace built for BOT Chain mainnet, chain six hundred and seventy-seven.

4
00:00:14,548 --> 00:00:16,980
Start with any deployed contract address.

5
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:20,336
Crash Lab retrieves the runtime bytecode that is actually on-chain.

6
00:00:20,336 --> 00:00:27,721
It records the code hash and runtime size, extracts selector candidates, and checks the EIP nineteen sixty-seven implementation slot for common proxy deployments.

7
00:00:27,721 --> 00:00:32,375
Analysis needs no wallet signature, submits no transaction, and never touches user funds.

8
00:00:32,375 --> 00:00:35,326
Next, the analyzer runs safe interface probes.

9
00:00:35,326 --> 00:00:42,432
It can recognize common token, NFT, vault, royalty, ownership, access-control, pause, permit, flash-loan, and multicall surfaces.

10
00:00:42,432 --> 00:00:49,557
Unknown applications still receive a universal bytecode and opcode review, so a custom contract is not rejected just because it does not match a popular standard.

11
00:00:49,557 --> 00:00:52,182
The deterministic layer is the source of truth.

12
00:00:52,182 --> 00:00:59,096
Every observation is stored as evidence: the live runtime fingerprint, the interface profile, the proxy result, and the executable opcode surface.

13
00:00:59,096 --> 00:01:01,432
A caution means review this behavior.

14
00:01:01,432 --> 00:01:07,009
It does not automatically mean the contract is exploitable, and a clean result is never presented as proof of safety.

15
00:01:07,009 --> 00:01:10,403
Then DeepSeek V four Flash becomes the investigation controller.

16
00:01:10,403 --> 00:01:17,653
The agent selects complementary read-only probes, receives only the evidence collected by Crash Lab, and must cite an exact evidence identifier for every finding.

17
00:01:17,653 --> 00:01:19,951
Unsupported citations are removed.

18
00:01:19,951 --> 00:01:24,538
It cannot publish a vulnerability claim, invent source code, or describe an exploit as proven.

19
00:01:24,538 --> 00:01:30,115
When the report is ready, the user can connect an EVM wallet and explicitly approve a zero-value BOT Chain transaction.

20
00:01:30,115 --> 00:01:32,644
The transaction calls no target contract.

21
00:01:32,644 --> 00:01:40,788
It anchors a versioned commitment containing the private analysis identifier and the exact AI report hash, creating a public timestamp and provenance trail without exposing the report itself.

22
00:01:40,788 --> 00:01:46,048
If the AI provider times out or returns invalid output, the investigation does not pretend everything is fine.

23
00:01:46,048 --> 00:01:53,500
Crash Lab switches to a clearly labeled deterministic evidence fallback, preserving the runtime observations and telling the reviewer that manual analysis is still required.

24
00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:55,826
Each browser gets a private scan ledger.

25
00:01:55,826 --> 00:02:00,086
You can reopen previous results without exposing another visitor's contract history.

26
00:02:00,086 --> 00:02:05,740
The interface also explains the report limits, the model source, confidence, review level, and every evidence item used.

27
00:02:05,740 --> 00:02:12,125
For the canonical crash scenario, the project also demonstrates donation-driven share inflation in an ERC forty-six twenty-six vault.

28
00:02:12,125 --> 00:02:16,471
A first depositor can inflate the share price so a later deposit rounds down to zero shares.

29
00:02:16,471 --> 00:02:21,076
The patched replay restores the invariant that every non-zero deposit must mint non-zero shares.

30
00:02:21,076 --> 00:02:25,307
The Simulation Passport anchors that exact canonical source and report on BOT Chain.

31
00:02:25,307 --> 00:02:29,826
It records the simulation identifier, hashes, publisher, transaction, and block.

32
00:02:29,826 --> 00:02:35,134
Wallet attestations prove individual AI reports existed, while the Passport proves the controlled replay record.

33
00:02:35,134 --> 00:02:38,500
Neither is a blanket security badge for unrelated contracts.

34
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:45,625
Crash Lab combines live chain evidence, explainable AI, wallet interaction, private scan history, and compact on-chain proof in one mobile-ready workflow.

35
00:02:45,625 --> 00:02:47,451
Inspect what is deployed.

36
00:02:47,451 --> 00:02:49,576
Understand what is observable.

37
00:02:49,576 --> 00:02:51,894
And before mainnet, crash it first.
